  "reason": "Evidence: config_048 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat) achieved a dominant 0.7207 accuracy, far exceeding all other configs (next best: 0.5988). This establishes scvi_n200 as the clear best RNA encoder and imagenet_vit_l as the best image encoder. The only untested variant within this top-performing family is the fusion method: config_050 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted). With pca_n2000, concat slightly outperformed weighted (0.5988 vs 0.5856), but the dynamics may differ with the richer scvi_n200 representations. This experiment tests whether weighted fusion could match or exceed concat in the best-performing architecture, directly clarifying the optimal fusion choice. It is the highest-value exploitation step: if weighted matches or beats concat, we find a new best; if not, we confirm config_048 as the optimal configuration and can focus remaining budget on confirming robustness. Expected cost is low (~4.5–4.7 GPU hours, comparable to config_047 and config_048), making it an efficient use of the next slot with 3 experiments remaining."
